@begin(section)

@title(Command Reference)

This guide describes the dsolv CLI: what subcommands and options there are,
and what they are for. It also describes how to specify options.

@begin(section)
@title(How Options Are Gathered)

dsolv is a @link[uri="https://github.com/djha-skin/cliff"](CLIFF)-powered
program. Options can be given via configuration files, environment variables,
and the command line, in that order, with later values overriding earlier
ones.

Configuration files are consulted from a system-wide location
(@c(/etc/dsolv/config.nrdl) on Linux), a home-directory location
(@c(~/.config/dsolv/config.nrdl) on Linux), and a file named @c(.dsolv.nrdl)
in the current directory (or any of its parents). Files can also be specified
explicitly with the @c(-c)/@c(--config-file) (NRDL) and
@c(-j)/@c(--json-config) (JSON) options. When multiple files are given, later
files override earlier ones.

Every option has a corresponding environment variable, named
@c(DSOLV_<KIND>_<OPTION>):

@begin(list)
@item(@c(DSOLV_FLAG_<OPTION>=1) enables a flag)
@item(@c(DSOLV_ITEM_<OPTION>=<VALUE>) sets a string value)
@item(@c(DSOLV_LIST_<OPTION>=<V1>,<V2>,...) sets a list option)
@item(@c(DSOLV_TABLE_<OPTION>=<K1>,<V1>=<K2>,<V2>=...) sets a key/value
table option)
@item(@c(DSOLV_NRDL_<OPTION>=<NRDL_STRING>) sets a value using a NRDL string)
@item(@c(DSOLV_FILE_<OPTION>=<FILE_PATH>) sets a value from a NRDL document
in a file, as if by the @c(--file-*) flag)
@item(@c(DSOLV_RAW_<OPTION>=<FILE_PATH>) sets a value from the raw bytes of a
file, as if by the @c(--raw-*) flag)
@end(list)

For compatibility with degasolv, the legacy @c(DEGASOLV_*) environment
variables are aliased to their @c(DSOLV_*) equivalents; for example,
@c(DEGASOLV_REQUIREMENTS) is an alias for @c(DSOLV_LIST_REQUIREMENTS) and
@c(DEGASOLV_CONFIG_FILES) for @c(DSOLV_LIST_CONFIG_FILES). The full alias
table is printed on the @c(help) page.

On the command line, each option can be set with a
@c(--set-<option> <value>) (string), @c(--add-<option> <value>) (list),
@c(--join-<option> <key>=<value>) (table), @c(--nrdl-<option> <nrdl>) (NRDL
string), or @c(--enable-<option>)/@c(--disable-<option>) (flag) form. The
legacy degasolv spellings (@c(--requirement), @c(--repository), @c(-r),
@c(-R), and so on) are provided as command line aliases, and are what the
rest of this guide uses.

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(A Note on Specifying Files)

Whenever an option takes a file, the user can specify one of four things:

@begin(enum)
@item(An @c(http://) or @c(https://) URL. URL-encoded authentication can be
specified before the @c(@) character:
@begin(list)
@item(@c(https://username:password@example.com/...) for HTTP basic
authentication)
@item(@c(https://token@example.com/...) for an OAuth2 bearer token)
@item(@c(https://X-Auth-Token=value@example.com/...) for a custom HTTP
header)
@end(list))
@item(A @c(file://) URL.)
@item(A plain filesystem reference.)
@item(The character @c(-), signifying standard input.)
@end(enum)

This is true for options of dsolv and options of any of its subcommands.

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Global Options)

These options are accepted by dsolv itself and are available to every
subcommand:

@begin(deflist)
@term(@c(-c), @c(--config-file @i(<file>)))
@def(Add an NRDL configuration file. May be specified multiple times; later
files override earlier ones. Environment: @c(DSOLV_LIST_CONFIG_FILES) /
@c(DEGASOLV_CONFIG_FILES).)
@term(@c(-j), @c(--json-config @i(<file>)))
@def(Add a JSON configuration file. May be specified multiple times;
later files override earlier ones. Environment:
@c(DSOLV_LIST_JSON_CONFIG_FILES) / @c(DEGASOLV_JSON_CONFIG_FILES).)
@term(@c(-k), @c(--option-pack @i(<pack>)))
@def(Apply an option pack, a bundle of default option values. Available
packs are @c(v1), @c(multi-version-mode), and @c(firstfound-version-mode)
(see @c(Strategies and Package Systems) below). May be specified multiple
times. Environment: @c(DSOLV_LIST_OPTION_PACKS) /
@c(DEGASOLV_OPTION_PACKS).)
@term(@c(-h), @c(--help), @c(help))
@def(Print the help page.)
@term(@c(--meta @i(<key>=<value>)))
@def(Set a metadata key/value pair. May be specified multiple times.
Environment: @c(DSOLV_TABLE_META).)
@end(deflist)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Strategies and Package Systems)

Several options control how resolution behaves. They are shared between
subcommands that resolve dependencies.

@begin(deflist)
@term(@c(-t), @c(--package-system @i(<system>)))
@def(The package system to use for slurping repositories. One of
@c(degasolv) (the default; @c(.dscard)/@c(.dsrepo) files),
@c(apt) (Debian @c(Packages.gz) indexes), @c(git) (a stub), or @c(subproc)
(an external executable). Environment:
@c(DSOLV_ITEM_PACKAGE_SYSTEM) / @c(DEGASOLV_PACKAGE_SYSTEM).)
@term(@c(-e), @c(--search-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Search strategy: @c(breadth-first) (default) or @c(depth-first).)
@term(@c(-f), @c(--conflict-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Conflict strategy: @c(exclusive) (default), @c(inclusive), or
@c(prioritized).)
@term(@c(-L), @c(--list-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(List strategy: @c(lazy) (default), @c(eager), or @c(as-set).)
@term(@c(-s), @c(--resolve-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Resolve strategy: @c(thorough) (default) or @c(fast).)
@term(@c(-S), @c(--index-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Index aggregation strategy: @c(priority) (default) or @c(global).)
@term(@c(-O), @c(--index-sort-order @i(<order>)))
@def(Sort order for repository index entries: @c(descending) (default) or
@c(ascending).)
@term(@c(-V), @c(--version-comparison @i(<scheme>)))
@def(The version comparison scheme: @c(debian), @c(maven), @c(naive),
@c(python), @c(rpm), @c(rubygem), or @c(semver) (the default). Provided by
the svers library.)
@term(@c(--enable-alternatives) / @c(--disable-alternatives))
@def(Whether to consider alternative versions of a package (default:
enabled). Environment: @c(DSOLV_FLAG_ALTERNATIVES) /
@c(DEGASOLV_ALTERNATIVES).)
@term(@c(--enable-error-format) / @c(--disable-error-format))
@def(Whether errors are printed as NRDL/JSON documents (default: disabled).
Environment: @c(DSOLV_FLAG_ERROR_FORMAT) / @c(DEGASOLV_ERROR_FORMAT).)
@term(@c(-o), @c(--output-format @i(<format>)))
@def(Output format: @c(plain) (default), @c(json), or @c(nrdl).)
@end(deflist)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Using Site-Wide Configuration Files)

The way configuration files are merged (see How Options Are Gathered above),
together with the fact that configuration files may be given as @c(http://)
or @c(https://) URLs (see A Note on Specifying Files above), makes it
possible to configure every dsolv installation in an organization from a
single, centrally served configuration file.

Several options fundamentally change how dsolv behaves: @c(--conflict-strat),
@c(--index-strat), @c(--resolve-strat), and @c(--search-strat) (see
Strategies and Package Systems above). It is recommended that these options
be specified site-wide, if they are specified at all. Putting them in a site
configuration file and serving that file internally over HTTP(S) lets each
build point at the site file together with its own build-specific
configuration, as in this example:

@begin[lang=sh](code)
dsolv \
    --config-file "https://nas.example.com/dsolv/site.nrdl" \
    --config-file "./.dsolv.nrdl" \
    generate-card
@end(code)

Remember that configuration files can also be specified with environment
variables. The example above looks like this when environment variables are
used, setting the @c(--config-file) option for every invocation:

@begin[lang=sh](code)
export DSOLV_LIST_CONFIG_FILES="https://nas.example.com/dsolv/site.nrdl,./.dsolv.nrdl"
dsolv generate-card
@end(code)

Here is the same example using JSON configuration files:

@begin[lang=sh](code)
export DSOLV_LIST_JSON_CONFIG_FILES="https://nas.example.com/dsolv/site.json,./.dsolv.json"
dsolv generate-card
@end(code)

For compatibility with degasolv, the legacy @c(DEGASOLV_CONFIG_FILES) and
@c(DEGASOLV_JSON_CONFIG_FILES) environment variables are aliases for
@c(DSOLV_LIST_CONFIG_FILES) and @c(DSOLV_LIST_JSON_CONFIG_FILES)
respectively.

As with any configuration that may contain passwords or API tokens (for
example, in the URLs of configuration files or repository indexes), decide
how sensitive information should reach dsolv. Options include environment
variables, standard input (@c(-) as the filename), configuration files with
appropriate filesystem permissions, or the command line itself; dsolv leaves
the choice of what is sufficiently secure to you.

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Subcommand: resolve-locations)

Resolve dependencies and print package locations. This is the heart of
dsolv: it takes requirements, a repository, and strategy options, and returns
the locations of the packages that satisfy the requirements.

Arguments used by @c(resolve-locations):

@begin(deflist)
@term(@c(-r), @c(--requirement @i(<req>)))
@def(Add a requirement, such as @c(a>2.0,<3.0) or @c(!b). May be specified
multiple times. Required. Environment:
@c(DSOLV_LIST_REQUIREMENTS) / @c(DEGASOLV_REQUIREMENTS).)
@term(@c(-R), @c(--repository @i(<url>)))
@def(Add a repository to consult. May be specified multiple times. Required
(unless the package system provides its own query constructor).
Environment: @c(DSOLV_LIST_REPOSITORIES) / @c(DEGASOLV_REPOSITORIES).)
@term(@c(-p), @c(--present-package @i(<id==version>)))
@def(Declare a package as already present in the build, in the form
@c(id==version). May be specified multiple times. Environment:
@c(DSOLV_LIST_PRESENT_PACKAGES) / @c(DEGASOLV_PRESENT_PACKAGES).)
@term(@c(-o), @c(--output-format @i(<format>)))
@def(Output format for the resolution result: @c(plain) (default),
@c(json), or @c(nrdl).)
@term(@c(-t), @c(--package-system @i(<system>)))
@def(The package system to use (see @c(Strategies and Package Systems)).)
@term(@c(-e), @c(--search-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Search strategy: @c(breadth-first) or @c(depth-first).)
@term(@c(-f), @c(--conflict-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Conflict strategy: @c(exclusive), @c(inclusive), or @c(prioritized).)
@term(@c(-L), @c(--list-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(List strategy: @c(lazy), @c(eager), or @c(as-set).)
@term(@c(-s), @c(--resolve-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Resolve strategy: @c(thorough) or @c(fast).)
@term(@c(-S), @c(--index-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Index aggregation strategy: @c(priority) or @c(global).)
@term(@c(-V), @c(--version-comparison @i(<scheme>)))
@def(Version comparison scheme (see @c(Strategies and Package Systems)).)
@term(@c(--enable-alternatives) / @c(--disable-alternatives))
@def(Whether to consider alternative versions of a package.)
@term(@c(--enable-error-format) / @c(--disable-error-format))
@def(Whether errors are printed as documents.)
@term(@c(-m), @c(--meta @i(<key>=<value>)))
@def(Set metadata on the result.)
@term(@c(-k), @c(--option-pack @i(<pack>)))
@def(Apply an option pack.)
@term(@c(-c), @c(--config-file @i(<file>)) and @c(-j), @c(--json-config @i(<file>)))
@def(Specify configuration files (see @c(Global Options)).)
@end(deflist)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Subcommand: generate-repo-index)

Generate a @c(.dsrepo) repository index from the @c(.dscard) files found
under a search directory.

Arguments used by @c(generate-repo-index):

@begin(deflist)
@term(@c(-d), @c(--search-directory @i(<dir>)))
@def(The directory to search for @c(.dscard) files. Default: @c(.).
Environment: @c(DSOLV_ITEM_SEARCH_DIRECTORY) /
@c(DEGASOLV_SEARCH_DIRECTORY).)
@term(@c(-I), @c(--index-file @i(<file>)))
@def(The index file to write. Default: @c(index.dsrepo). Environment:
@c(DSOLV_ITEM_INDEX_FILE) / @c(DEGASOLV_INDEX_FILE).)
@term(@c(-a), @c(--add-to @i(<file>)))
@def(If given, an existing index to merge the new entries into, rather than
starting from an empty index.)
@term(@c(-O), @c(--index-sort-order @i(<order>)))
@def(Sort order for the index entries: @c(descending) (default) or
@c(ascending).)
@term(@c(-V), @c(--version-comparison @i(<scheme>)))
@def(Version comparison scheme used for sorting. Default: @c(semver).)
@end(deflist)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Subcommand: generate-card)

Generate a @c(.dscard) file representing a package in a dsolv repository.

Arguments used by @c(generate-card):

@begin(deflist)
@term(@c(-i), @c(--id @i(<id>)))
@def(The package id. Required. Environment: @c(DSOLV_ITEM_ID) /
@c(DEGASOLV_ID).)
@term(@c(-v), @c(--version @i(<version>)))
@def(The package version. Required. Environment: @c(DSOLV_ITEM_VERSION) /
@c(DEGASOLV_VERSION).)
@term(@c(-l), @c(--location @i(<url>)))
@def(Where the package artifact can be downloaded. Required. Environment:
@c(DSOLV_ITEM_LOCATION) / @c(DEGASOLV_LOCATION).)
@term(@c(-r), @c(--requirement @i(<req>)))
@def(Add a requirement of this package. May be specified multiple times.)
@term(@c(-m), @c(--meta @i(<key>=<value>)))
@def(Set additional metadata fields on the card. Keys that conflict with the
card's built-in fields (@c(id), @c(version), @c(location),
@c(requirements)) are ignored.)
@term(@c(-C), @c(--card-file @i(<file>)))
@def(Where to write the card. Default: @c(./out.dscard). Environment:
@c(DSOLV_ITEM_CARD_FILE) / @c(DEGASOLV_CARD_FILE).)
@end(deflist)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Subcommand: query-repo)

Query a repository for the packages matching a query, without resolving.

Arguments used by @c(query-repo):

@begin(deflist)
@term(@c(-R), @c(--repository @i(<url>)))
@def(Add a repository to query. May be specified multiple times. Required.)
@term(@c(-q), @c(--query @i(<query>)))
@def(The query, a requirement such as @c(e) or @c(e>=1.8.0). Required.
Environment: @c(DSOLV_ITEM_QUERY) / @c(DEGASOLV_QUERY).)
@term(@c(-S), @c(--index-strat @i(<strat>)))
@def(Index aggregation strategy: @c(priority) or @c(global).)
@term(@c(-o), @c(--output-format @i(<format>)))
@def(Output format: @c(plain), @c(json), or @c(nrdl).)
@term(@c(-t), @c(--package-system @i(<system>)))
@def(The package system to use.)
@term(@c(-V), @c(--version-comparison @i(<scheme>)))
@def(Version comparison scheme.)
@term(@c(--enable-error-format) / @c(--disable-error-format))
@def(Whether an empty result set is reported as an error document.)
@end(deflist)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Subcommand: display-config)

Display the effective configuration, after merging configuration files,
environment variables, and the command line.

Arguments used by @c(display-config):

@begin(deflist)
@term(@c(-o), @c(--output-format @i(<format>)))
@def(Output format: @c(plain), @c(json), or @c(nrdl).)
@term(@c(-c), @c(--config-file @i(<file>)) and @c(-j), @c(--json-config @i(<file>)))
@def(Specify configuration files whose effective contents should be shown.)
@end(deflist)

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(The Default Action)

Running @c(dsolv) with no subcommand prints a short usage message and the
list of available subcommands. To learn more about a specific subcommand,
run @c(dsolv <subcommand> help) or pass @c(--enable-help).

@end(section)

@begin(section)
@title(Notes on Versions)

@begin(list)
@item(On a best-effort basis, features have had the version that they first
appeared associated with them in this guide.)
@item(As of version 1.3.0 of degasolv (whose CLI dsolv mirrors), all options
which take a file may be given @c(-) as the filename to specify standard
input. dsolv inherits this behavior.)
@end(list)

@end(section)

@end(section)
